ACPICA chooses its host's configuration by the compiler's and the
system's names in acenv.h. This names ThreadOS (__THREADOS__, which the
Makefile defines) and its header, kernel/acpica/acthreados.h - the only
change to ACPICA. It comes first: the compiler that builds the kernel
is a Linux one and says __linux__, which would otherwise pick ACPICA's
Linux host - one with a C library.

--- a/source/include/platform/acenv.h
+++ b/source/include/platform/acenv.h
@@ -305,7 +305,10 @@
 
 #endif
 
-#if defined(_LINUX) || defined(__linux__)
+#if defined(__THREADOS__)
+#include "acthreados.h"
+
+#elif defined(_LINUX) || defined(__linux__)
 #include "aclinux.h"
 
 #elif defined(_APPLE) || defined(__APPLE__)
